# Story: paused for a film in full screen. The Mac's privacy daemon restarts: for a second Arbor doubts its Accessibility permission, and the doubt
# passes by itself. Nobody granted anything, so nothing ends: the pause goes on, no window moves, the keys stay given away, and what the pause
# still owes is still paid: the window that was in full screen comes into view when the film is over (F63, criterion 7; board 0.21).
open Safari
open Mail
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
zoom 101
expect hidden 102
fullscreen 102 on
pause
expect ok
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+escape on
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+left off
wait 5
revoke
wait 2.6
status
expect replied taken away
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+left off
grant
wait 1
expect still
status
expect replied paused
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+escape on
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+left off
key ctrl+opt+left
expect app-got ctrl+opt+left
expect silent
fullscreen 102 off where-it-was
wait 10
expect visible 102
expect visible 101
# The one thing that counts in a doubt is the person's own word.
revoke
wait 2.6
key ctrl+opt+escape
expect fail
expect said Arbor needs the Accessibility permission
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+left on
grant
wait 1
status
expect replied running
expect silent
expect count docked 2
